RF filters are essential components within radio-frequency front-end systems. They help select desired frequency ranges while suppressing unwanted signals, supporting the performance of wireless devices operating across multiple communication bands. Bulk Acoustic Wave (BAW), Surface Acoustic Wave (SAW), and Integrated Passive Device (IPD) technologies serve different requirements involving frequency, insertion loss, integration, and device design.

